Title: The Significance of Boredom: A Literature Review
Abstract: This article provides a comprehensive overview of the significance of boredom and argues that boredom is a phenomenon worthy of interdisciplinary research. It examines the prevalence of boredom, its social consequences, its functions, and its potentially positive outcomes. The article discusses boredom across different spheres of human life and considers its connections with cognition, motivation, communication, consumerism, reflection, self-knowledge, creativity, and cultural production.
Keywords: boredom, boredom studies, emotions, significance of boredom, interdisciplinary, functions of boredom
